(text "Sheet 4: gate drivers, current sense and fault comparators" (at 25.4 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid cc99eca8-f41b-5faf-b24e-1df372f35f87))
(text "Fault thresholds (dividers from +5V):\nREF_A 0.114 V = 3.4 A in R13 (boost switch)\nREF_B 1.92 V = 43.3 V on VLED\nREF_C 1.39 V = 6.9 A charge current\nREF_D 1.48 V = 15.0 V battery" (at 284.48 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 29dbcd26-2159-505e-b403-30a821c4d5c3))
(text "U2 LM2901: open-collector outputs wired together on FLT (U1 pin 24, active low, latched, 1 us filter). Signal on -, threshold on +, so a fault pulls FLT low." (at 25.4 185.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 92275f61-8e99-5505-b9b0-33f06335f307))
(text "Notes\n- R29, R30, R33: PWM pins go high-impedance on a FLT fault; these keep the drivers off.\n- U4 HS pin is SW_C (sheet 1). C36 is the bootstrap cap, 100 nF (UCC27211 datasheet: 22-100 nF typical).\n- U7 split outputs: R34 sets turn-on speed, R35 turn-off.\n- U5: charge current 5.8 A -> 1.16 V, 7 A -> 1.40 V.  U6: LED current 0.565 A -> 1.13 V.\n- U6 IN- (pin 4) must be Kelvin-routed to the ground pad of R14, not to the nearest ground." (at 25.4 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1ec2e77f-3062-51f9-8621-8adfd973cbd9))
)
